{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAPER-CHECK-D751.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Paper check of council 67's wording on the stored replies (before any change or send)\n     2\t\n     3\t**The proposed wording** (council 67, `codex-r67.md` item 6) would replace the opening sentence of the final evidence check\n     4\t(`judging-v13s.txt` line 9): \"When other evidence bears on the forecast, say which band it favours before choosing any adjustment.\n     5\tIf that choice depends on a fact the passages leave open, explain why one band is more likely across the plausible readings, or\n     6\tanswer unresolved and name the missing fact.\" The existing routes stay: a supported size, a bound, or an explained comparison.\n     7\t\n     8\t**What the check must show (council 67, item 7):**\n     9\t- it exposes the unsupported premises in the $42B and $35B answers;\n    10\t- it preserves the two specific \"can't tell\" answers;\n    11\t- it explains the disputed $37B answer without declaring every forecast near a cutoff wrong.\n    12\t\n    13\tIf it cannot, the wording is dropped and the default question goes to Alex.\n    14\t\n    15\t**The fact E's 15 passages leave open:** whether the volume for FY2028 is in hand. That covers commercial shipment status and the\n    16\tsize of any execution shortfall against the unsized \"more than\" in \"more than double\".\n    17\t\n    18\t## The eight stored E replies\n    19\t\n    20\t| Run | Writer | Answer | Depends on an open fact? | Under the wording | Recorded readings |\n    21\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    22\t| third run | Codex | 85% realisation → $34B, rung 3 | yes: the size of a shortfall | exposed: the cut's size is asserted, not explained across readings | settled no |\n    23\t| third run | Claude (T15) | 1.85x bracket, Vera as all CPU → $37B, rung 3 | yes: whether execution falls short of \"more than double\" | not settled by the words alone: it explains why adoption beats the market pace and why evaluation and competition temper doubling, but not why rung 3 beats rung 2 if the volume is in hand. A boundary answer, consistent with its history (accepted, then split) | yes, yes; split under D747 |\n    24\t| targeted | Codex (U05) | 90% realisation → $36B | yes: the size of a shortfall | exposed | settled no |\n    25\t| targeted | Claude (U06) | 1.8x × 90% Vera share → $32.4B | yes: the pace and the Vera share | exposed: two unexplained assumptions; its own lower anchor gives $27B | settled no |\n    26\t| D749 | Codex | unresolved: the base and the increase are projections; no run-rate, units, prices or schedule | names the open fact | preserved | settled yes |\n    27\t| D749 | Claude (X05) | 2.1x in full → $42B, rung 2, \"already selling at volume\" | yes: it asserts the open fact instead of explaining across readings | exposed | split |\n    28\t| D750 | Codex | unresolved: the base is a target; no shipments, schedules, units or prices | names the open fact | preserved | settled yes |\n    29\t| D750 | Claude (X06) | 1.75x midpoint of market pace and doubling → $35B, rung 3 | yes: the shortfall size; it also treats a minimum as a ceiling | exposed | settled no |\n    30\t\n    31\t## Forecasts near a cutoff that the wording must not condemn (S and P-v8)\n    32\t\n    33\t- **D750 S Codex** ($692.9–737.6B, central about $715B), **D750 S Claude** ($708.1B) and **D749 S Codex** ($730B).\n    34\t  - Their band depends on an open fact: the data-center share of the four companies' spending.\n    35\t  - Each explains why rung 4 is more likely across readings. It treats the AI-infrastructure plan as a plan that can slip, states\n    36\t    the slip that would be needed (more than $30–45B outside data centers), and gives the evidence against such a slip.\n    37\t  - Under the wording they stand. All were settled supported.\n    38\t- **P-v8 answers** are not near a cutoff, since every reading in the bounds shown keeps rung 2. The wording leaves them as they are.\n    39\t\n    40\t## Result of the paper check (Claude's reading; for the council to verify independently)\n    41\t\n    42\t- **Exposes both target answers:** $42B and $35B, yes.\n    43\t- **Preserves both \"can't tell\" answers:** yes.\n    44\t- **The $37B answer** stays a boundary answer. The words tell its writer what was missing: why rung 3 if the volume is in hand. They\n    45\t  do not declare it wrong by fiat.\n    46\t- **Explained near-cutoff forecasts** on S stand.\n    47\t- **It does not resolve the reference-labelling objection** on D750 S Claude (a total-capex range marked as the data-center\n    48\t  reference). That is a separate class, recorded as an open defect, and is not addressed by this wording.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r67.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t1. **Serious — E repeats one mistake.** I recommend **(b), one change to how the writer chooses a forecast, followed by one $0 test.** On the same 15 passages, the D749 Claude writer said Vera was already selling at volume and forecast $42B. The D750 writer read future deployments as grounds for a discount and forecast $35B. The passages establish management’s expectation, a customer evaluation and a working platform. They establish neither commercial shipment status nor the volume secured for FY2028. The recurring mistake is letting an unknown fact decide which side of $40B to publish. Across four runs Claude forecast $37B, $32.4B, $42B and $35B. None earned settled support under the current definitions. Codex’s last two answers named the missing fact and both were accepted. [E passages:9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/E/user.txt:9) · [D749 Claude answer:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/E/answers/claude.json:1) · [D750 Codex answer:83](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/E/answers/codex.json:83) · [Four-run record:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND6-RESULT.md:40)\n     2\t\n     3\t2. **Serious — the two instructions pull in different directions, but neither licenses the $35B answer.** Guidance governs when it stands alone. The discount applies to a product that has yet to ship. E has other evidence, and that evidence leaves shipment status open. The writer nevertheless used market growth as NVIDIA’s floor, management’s “more than double” as a ceiling, and the midpoint as its forecast. Even its lower comparison, about 1.48 × $20B = $29.6B, falls outside its chosen $30–40B band. Both adjudicators rejected the forecast. The writer’s later account confirms which instructions pulled it toward a discount. Its later preference for management’s band is a retrospective opinion. D749’s $42B answer also depended on an unsupported claim about sales. Neither establishes that keeping guidance would pass. [Request:4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4) · [D750 Claude answer:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/E/answers/claude.json:1) · [Claude adjudication:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/adjudication/X06.claude.json:1) · [Codex adjudication:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/adjudication/X06.codex.json:5) · [Writer’s account:13](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r67.md:13)\n     4\t\n     5\t3. **Serious — the paid run can still decide whether calculating related answers together helps.** It scores 36 first attempts as 9 joint pairs, 9 reconciled separate pairs and 9 singletons. There are exactly two ways to clear the pair thresholds: **8 usable joint pairs with at most 5 usable separate pairs, or 9 with at most 6**. Each snapshot must supply at least 2 of 3 usable joint pairs. If the separate calculation gets 7, even a perfect joint result cannot pass. A supported P-v8 answer alone says nothing about that gain. O, S and E contribute zero pairs to the gain, but one published contradiction, internal reference or gap that decides the band on any joint or singleton answer stops a complete run. A singleton’s unsupported vote alone does not stop it. An unresolved singleton is published and inspected too. The proxy results establish neither Luna’s stop rate nor an inevitable stop. A pass earns production **design**. Alex explicitly kept the paid re-send on hold pending a clean $0 pass. D749 was inconclusive and D750 failed, so option (a) would require him to waive that condition. Option (d) would abandon a comparison that can still decide something. [Paid plan:9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:9) · [Verdict code:772](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:772) · [Singleton rule:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND4-RESULT.md:69) · [Meaning of a pass:278](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:278) · [Alex’s condition:11651](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11651)\n     6\t\n     7\t4. **Minor for the next decision — one S objection is a real labeling defect.** I would reject the 104% mark. The format calls for both extremes of a ratio, and $130B divided by $125–145B gives 89.7–104%. The answer uses about 96% at the midpoint and never forecasts Meta spending 104% of its total. I would uphold the reference objection. The source explicitly says **total** capital spending, with a large portion going to AI. The writer marked that entire range as the market’s reference for **data-center** spending. The figure passes the source check, but Alex’s rule also requires an outside reference for the quantity asked. The writer’s separate 3% deduction supports its own forecast and cannot turn the source into a market estimate for the narrower quantity. The registered marks remain split. Resolving both would still leave E’s settled failure. Also, the paid S case is for 2027, while X08 is for 2026. [Ratio rule:79](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/reader-packets/X08.md:79) · [Ratio as written:589](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/reader-packets/X08.md:589) · [Source quote:177](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/reader-packets/X08.md:177) · [Reference designation:355](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/reader-packets/X08.md:355) · [Alex’s ruling:11356](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11356) · [Paid cases:43](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:43)\n     8\t\n     9\t5. **Wording — qualify the claim that S converged.** D750’s two fresh S forecasts earned support, with the two defect marks above still split. D749’s corrected X08 **support** verdict was itself split: one reader accepted $710.4B while treating $730B as a floor. “All four supported” overstates the corrected record. [D749 correction:8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND5-RESULT.md:8) · [D750 results:12](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND6-RESULT.md:12) · [Claude’s reflection:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r67.md:5)\n    10\t\n    11\t6. **One recommendation — put the choice before the calculation.** Keep the existing guidance-alone rule. Replace the opening sentence of the final evidence check with this wording: **“When other evidence bears on the forecast, say which band it favours before choosing any adjustment. If that choice depends on a fact the passages leave open, explain why one band is more likely across the plausible readings, or answer unresolved and name the missing fact.”** Keep the existing routes for a supported size, bound or explained comparison. This applies equally to a launch, a spending share or a growth estimate. It permits a forecast when the uncertainty leaves one band more likely. It also addresses both the unsupported assertion of sales and the unsupported discount. Option (c) becomes necessary if the intended product behavior is to publish management’s band by default in that situation. D746 explicitly reserves that choice for Alex. [Current final check:9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:9) · [Indirect comparisons allowed:11581](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11581) · [Product-choice boundary:11566](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11566)\n    12\t\n    13\t7. **One test — first check the distinction on paper, then obtain one fresh blind result.** Before sending anything, apply the proposed words to all eight stored E replies. They must expose the unsupported premises in both $42B and $35B, preserve the two specific “can’t tell” answers, and explain the earlier disputed $37B answer without declaring every forecast near a cutoff wrong. If the wording cannot do that, drop it and take the default question to Alex. If it can, have the council register **one** $0 writer test under the existing terms: both writer families on E, S and P-v8, with the invented cut and impossible floor as controls. Only a clean pass moves the decision to Alex for paid authorization. A settled failure or persistent split ends this wording loop and returns the publication choice to him. This review used stored material only and made no edits or sends. [Registered cases and controls:463](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:463) · [Pass conditions:480](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:480) · [Decision after the test:533](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:533)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND6-RESULT.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The D750 second writer test: result\n     2\t\n     3\tRun folder: `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/`. It was registered in `SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D750], with council round 66's\n     4\tchanges, and scored by `blind6.py tally` (`TALLY.json`, `reasons.json`). The request is `judging-v13s.txt`, sha256 `54f5847d…`.\n     5\t\n     6\t## 1. Verdict: FAIL on one settled line\n     7\t\n     8\t| Packet | Answer | Shape, rung | First readers (Codex, Claude) | Adjudicators (Codex, Claude) | Settled | Line |\n     9\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    10\t| X06 | fresh E Claude | forecast, rung 3 ($35B: 1.75x pace) | yes, no | no, no | **no** | **FAIL** |\n    11\t| X07 | fresh E Codex | unresolved | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    12\t| X05 | fresh S Codex | forecast, rung 4 ($692.9–737.6B, central about $715B) | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    13\t| X08 | fresh S Claude | forecast, rung 4 ($708.1B: $715–745B × 97%) | yes, yes; Codex marked two defects | defects: uphold, reject | yes; two defect splits | inconclusive |\n    14\t| X02 | fresh P-v8 Claude | forecast, rung 2 ($385.9B) | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    15\t| X04 | fresh P-v8 Codex | forecast, rung 2 ($377.7B) | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    16\t| X03 | control: invented 10% cut | forecast | no, no | (none) | no | ok |\n    17\t| X01 | control: impossible floor | forecast | floor marked by both | (support only) | floor settled | ok |\n    18\t\n    19\t- **The failure.** X06's writer took the market pace (about 1.48–1.5x) as a floor and management's \"more than double\" as a\n    20\t  ceiling, and chose 1.75x, the midpoint.\n    21\t  - Both adjudicators: the passages state \"more than double\" as a minimum; the midpoint has no source; the reasons for a miss\n    22\t    (one customer evaluating, a competitor's own benchmarks, missing volume figures) size or bound no shortfall below $40B. The\n    23\t    answer shows only that the outcome might fall short.\n    24\t- **The defect splits on X08.**\n    25\t  - F15 = 130 ÷ (125–145) gives a range whose top end is 104%. The Codex adjudicator calls that a part above its whole. The Claude\n    26\t    adjudicator calls it the mechanical end of a range ratio that the format requires.\n    27\t  - F5, the outside total-capex range, is marked as the market's reference for data-center spending. The Codex adjudicator says this\n    28\t    implies a 100% share. The Claude adjudicator says F5 is a quoted outside figure, as the reference rule allows, and that the\n    29\t    deduction is set out separately.\n    30\t- **The reasons and premises** behind every settled S and E vote were read and recorded (`reasons.json`). X05 and X08's readers read\n    31\t  the same four companies' AI-infrastructure plan as a plan that can slip, not as a floor, which fits each answer's own outcome.\n    32\t- **A run incident, disclosed.** The background command running the eight Codex readers was terminated (exit 144) while three\n    33\t  readers were still running. X04, X05 and X08 had empty outputs, kept in `reader-packets/interrupted/`. Fresh Codex readers were\n    34\t  run for those three. No reading was discarded after it was seen.\n    35\t\n    36\t## 2. The E record across the four runs (same case, same passages)\n    37\t\n    38\t| Run | Codex writer | Claude writer |\n    39\t|---|---|---|\n    40\t| third run (D742 request) | 85% realisation, $34B; settled no | 1.85x bracket, $37B; yes in re-read 2, split under D747 |\n    41\t| targeted test (D745) | 90% realisation, $36B; settled no | 1.8x × 90% share, $32.4B; split, then no under D747 |\n    42\t| D749 | unresolved, specific gap; settled yes | 2.1x in full, $42B, asserting \"already selling at volume\"; split |\n    43\t| D750 | unresolved, specific gap; settled yes | 1.75x bracket midpoint, $35B; settled no |\n    44\t\n    45\t- **The Codex writer.** The repair (D749, D750) moved it from invented cuts to a justified unresolved, twice.\n    46\t- **The Claude writer.** It forecasts every time, by a different route each time, and has never been settled supported under the\n    47\t  current definitions.\n    48\t- **S** improved but did not fully settle (corrected after council 67):\n    49\t  - D750's two fresh forecasts earned settled support, with two defect marks on X08 still split.\n    50\t  - D749's X08 support verdict was split after the correction: one reader accepted $710.4B while treating $730B as a floor.\n    51\t  - D749's S Codex was settled supported.\n    52\t- **P-v8** has been supported throughout.\n    53\t\n    54\t## 3. Not done\n    55\t\n    56\tNothing was paid. Nothing was tuned on the 36 stored answers. The request was not changed after the registration.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
